		{
			"id": "taLj4HX-oq_z565ck",
			"name": "Aeldari Psyker (Talent)",
			"reference": "TSOR5",
			"local_notes": "Identical chassis and cost to Imperium/Psykers and the Warp.adq's\nPsyker (Talent, itself the Sorcery Talent analogue, TSOR5, 10/level):\nadds its level to Psyniscience, Meditation, Hidden Lore (the Warp),\nand the Will roll to resist Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes).\nReflavoured off the Adeptus Astra Telepathica's Imperium-specific\nAssignment scale, which doesn't apply to a species with no Black Ships\nand no Scholastia Psykana: Aeldari psychic strength is instead judged\nby how far along the Path of the Seer someone has travelled.\n  Untrained latent (every Aeldari) — Talent 0\n  Path of the Seer apprentice — Talent 1-2\n  Warlock — Talent 2-3 (still primarily a warrior and squad leader)\n  Farseer — Talent 5 (Codex background's own \"psyker of the highest grade\")\n\nLore: What actually separates a Warlock or Farseer from any other Aeldari's shared latent Psychic Sensitivity: years spent under a Seer Council's supervision, sharpening the same faculties (Psyniscience, Meditation, Hidden Lore of the Warp, and self-control against Perils) that a human Sanctioned Psyker's own Psyker Talent sharpens, before either setting the gift aside or being claimed by the Path of the Seer entirely.\n\nDesign: Talent affecting four things (three skills plus the Perils resistance roll), the same Medium Talent rate (B90, 10 points/level) Imperium's Psyker (Talent) and this project's Ork Kunnin'/Mek Instinct/Painboy's Eye all use for the same reason. Capped at level 6 for player characters, matching the Imperium trait's own cap.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Talent",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 2,
			"base_points": 0,
			"max_levels": 6
		},
		{
			"id": "tJ_mWSV78_MIbJWMb",
			"name": "Aeldari Warp Empowerment",
			"reference": "TSOR4",
			"local_notes": "Identical chassis and cost to Imperium/Psykers and the Warp.adq's\nWarp Empowerment (itself the Sorcerous Empowerment analogue, TSOR4, 10\nbase + 10/level): the same cap rule applies unchanged — an Aeldari may\nonly know a Rune whose full, modified point cost is no greater than\nthe point cost of their own Aeldari Warp Empowerment. Requires Aeldari\nPsychic Sensitivity.\n\nRough Path-of-the-Seer mapping, worked out the same way Imperium's\nWarp Empowerment notes work out its own Assignment-grade table, from\nthis file's actual (Warp Sorcery -20% + Perils of the Warp, Aeldari\nRunes) modified costs:\n  Level      | Cap (10+10/lvl) | What the cap reaches\n  1          | 20              | most Runes of Battle basics and most single-level Runes of Fate at their starting level\n  2-3        | 30-40           | the non-attack Runes of Fate and the Runes of Battle basics (each 19 or less) with headroom\n  6          | 70              | Destructor at its full 7 dice (62) plus every other Rune of Battle — typical Warlock ceiling\n  10         | 110             | Eldritch Storm at its full 8 dice (108)\n  21         | 220             | Executioner at its full 10 dice (213): the Farseer's killing stroke — typical Farseer ceiling\nThe attack Runes (Executioner, Eldritch Storm, Destructor) are built\nat lore scale rather than party scale, so their caps are far above\nthe rest of the roster; a psyker who knows only the small Runes buys\nonly the level those need. A Warlock is far below a Farseer's\nceiling: see each template's own notes for the level it actually buys.\n\nLore: What actually gates a Rune of Battle or Rune of Fate is not raw willingness to learn it, in Codex background's own telling, but how much of the warp a given Aeldari's own training and discipline let them safely hold open at once — a Warlock's working repertoire is genuinely smaller than a Farseer's, not merely less-often used.\n\nDesign: Identical cost structure to Sorcerous Empowerment/Imperium's Warp Empowerment (10 base + 10/level): the underlying mechanic — \"how much of the warp you can safely channel at all, gating which Runes you may know by their modified cost\" — is exactly the same chassis, just judged by Path progress instead of an Imperial Assignment grade.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Talent",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 6,
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "t-Larw70J1AIr-QJM",
			"name": "Aeldari Soul-Sense",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Aeldari analogue of Witch-sight: an unlearned, passive prickling awareness of psychic activity, daemonic taint and warp corruption, sharpened rather than granted outright by walking the Path of the Seer even partway.\n\nDesign: Built exactly as Imperium/Psykers and the Warp.adq's Witch-sight: Detect (Psychic Activity & Daemonic Taint), base 10 (B47-48), Warp Sorcery -20% only (no Perils: involuntary background sense, not a deliberate act). Full modified cost: 10 x 0.8 = 8 points; needs only Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "mwrOSwUAhUETzx7kb",
					"name": "Warp Sorcery",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				}
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "TW7ZIniEFjKgCvo1T",
			"name": "Runes of Battle",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Runes of Battle are a Warlock's working repertoire: simpler, more reliable than a Farseer's Runes of Fate, and cast in the thick of a fight to protect the squad, blind the enemy, or turn either against the foe instead. Every pair below is one Rune worked in two opposite directions, per Codex background's own pairing of Conceal/Reveal, Protect/Jinx, and Enhance/Drain.\n\nDesign: Talent-linked group; see each child pair.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "TMLWeTsCqvWxtzstK",
					"name": "Conceal/Reveal",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The same Rune of Battle worked two ways: a soft shimmer that hides a squad from sight, or the same working turned outward to strip a hidden enemy's cover away.\n\nDesign: Alternative_abilities container; full price for the costlier Reveal plus a fifth of the cheaper Conceal.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari",
						"Psyker"
					],
					"container_type": "alternative_abilities",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tHHDy1AobSd02ILEc",
							"name": "Conceal",
							"local_notes": "Lore: A shimmer of bent light and muffled sound over a willing ally, easing a squad's approach unseen.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10) delivering a +10 point Stealth-boosting advantage, Warp Sorcery (-20%), Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Net -15%. Full modified cost: 10 x 0.85 = 8.5, rounded up to 9 points (discounted to a fifth as the cheaper alternative ability, so the container costs 19 + 2 = 21); needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20) at its full-price rate.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Xenos",
								"Aeldari",
								"Psyker"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mdv7DEts4tIByR1Po",
									"name": "Advantage Delivered (Concealed",
									"cost_adj": "+10%"
								},
								{
									"id": "m43laculvKxVHhf7j",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mSwv2UKUIUgVpzeGa",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
									"cost_adj": "-5%"
								}
							],
							"base_points": 10
						},
						{
							"id": "tgfYy2ydztndnxNB2",
							"name": "Reveal",
							"local_notes": "Lore: Strips an enemy's own concealment, camouflage, or holo-field away in an instant.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10) delivering a -10 point \"Exposed\" disadvantage, Malediction (+100%), Warp Sorcery (-20%), Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Net +85%. Full modified cost: 10 x 1.85 = 18.5, rounded to 19 points (the costlier child, so it sets the container's cap requirement); needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Xenos",
								"Aeldari",
								"Psyker"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mtSmschMx4Oa2lhOr",
									"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Exposed",
									"cost_adj": "+10%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mCNltWoOHL0BhbZ2w",
									"name": "Malediction 1",
									"cost_adj": "+100%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mRfi6wvVfozlz-sa_",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mcfCVEr0Mg0o_i7T1",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
									"cost_adj": "-5%"
								}
							],
							"base_points": 10
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "TF0l5Gyy-SckpMKLJ",
					"name": "Protect/Jinx",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The same Rune worked as a shield for an ally, or a curse that strips an enemy's own defences thin.\n\nDesign: Alternative_abilities container; full price for the costlier Jinx plus a fifth of the cheaper Protect.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari",
						"Psyker"
					],
					"container_type": "alternative_abilities",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tcncu7bVS5T_BNBu4",
							"name": "Protect",
							"local_notes": "Lore: A brief, hardening ward of psychic force over a willing ally, thickening their guard for a few crucial seconds.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10) delivering a +10 point DR-boosting advantage, Warp Sorcery (-20%), Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Net -15%. Full modified cost: 8.5, rounded up to 9 points (discounted to a fifth as the cheaper alternative ability, so the container costs 19 + 2 = 21); needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20) at its full-price rate.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Xenos",
								"Aeldari",
								"Psyker"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "m9LuUii85DUJiyuC8",
									"name": "Advantage Delivered (Warded",
									"cost_adj": "+10%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mx9ieWLiTPRr3wauN",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "m0s_I8PO0aNyVgxpX",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
									"cost_adj": "-5%"
								}
							],
							"base_points": 10
						},
						{
							"id": "tLGb_5akVtNoxZ_g1",
							"name": "Jinx",
							"local_notes": "Lore: Curses an enemy's own guard thin at the worst possible moment.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10) delivering a -10 point defense-penalty disadvantage, Malediction (+100%), Warp Sorcery (-20%), Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Net +85%. Full modified cost: 18.5, rounded to 19 points (the costlier child, so it sets the container's cap requirement); needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Xenos",
								"Aeldari",
								"Psyker"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mLM_joU2iaU0yrKDT",
									"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Jinxed",
									"cost_adj": "+10%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mgcddRT4rELzU6H7G",
									"name": "Malediction 1",
									"cost_adj": "+100%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mvOZCM91E_d8WDOj6",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mc80trtXVBhKPtCng",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
									"cost_adj": "-5%"
								}
							],
							"base_points": 10
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "TeWUw5yois_vuCr96",
					"name": "Enhance/Drain",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The same Rune worked as a surge of strength for an ally, or a draining curse that saps an enemy's own.\n\nDesign: Alternative_abilities container; full price for the costlier Drain plus a fifth of the cheaper Enhance.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari",
						"Psyker"
					],
					"container_type": "alternative_abilities",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tX9X0ePwWS3bC7yQe",
							"name": "Enhance",
							"local_notes": "Lore: A surge of psychically-lent strength or speed into a willing ally's limbs.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10) delivering a +10 point ST/DX-boosting advantage, Warp Sorcery (-20%), Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Net -15%. Full modified cost: 8.5, rounded up to 9 points (discounted to a fifth as the cheaper alternative ability, so the container costs 19 + 2 = 21); needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20) at its full-price rate.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Physical",
								"Xenos",
								"Aeldari",
								"Psyker"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mAibOVPIs_TM3dZHu",
									"name": "Advantage Delivered (Enhanced",
									"cost_adj": "+10%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mHcoNvjt8HEN10Vb7",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mnI3FmJ3SVn6rhx0y",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
									"cost_adj": "-5%"
								}
							],
							"base_points": 10
						},
						{
							"id": "t4NYBcUpivIWYhFsF",
							"name": "Drain",
							"local_notes": "Lore: Saps the strength or endurance straight out of an enemy's limbs.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10) delivering a -10 point ST/DX/FP-draining disadvantage, Malediction (+100%), Warp Sorcery (-20%), Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Net +85%. Full modified cost: 18.5, rounded to 19 points (the costlier child, so it sets the container's cap requirement); needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Xenos",
								"Aeldari",
								"Psyker"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mk3Zf0TI-nj-XXclW",
									"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Drained",
									"cost_adj": "+10%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mKnsPTvXDeSe_Pdxb",
									"name": "Malediction 1",
									"cost_adj": "+100%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mqN_vk1igjsPgblxH",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mnGyLxBGALppsXoGw",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
									"cost_adj": "-5%"
								}
							],
							"base_points": 10
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "Tk-HNGak9SxlU3oEZ",
					"name": "Destructor/Embolden",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The Warlock's two most iconic Runes of Battle: Destructor, a flame-blast of psychic fire flung at the enemy, and Embolden, the same power turned inward to fill the squad with fearless resolve.\n\nDesign: Alternative_abilities container; full price for the costlier Destructor plus a fifth of the cheaper Embolden.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari",
						"Psyker"
					],
					"container_type": "alternative_abilities",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tJCPAF5SziAnEfluN",
							"name": "Destructor",
							"local_notes": "Lore: A blast of psychic flame that bursts on the target and scorches everything nearby.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Burning, 5/die, B61) bought at 7 levels, 7d(2) burn ex, with Explosion (+50%, B106, 2-yard burst, as this project's Imperium Inferno), Armor Divisor (2) (+50%, B102), Warp Sorcery (-20%) and Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Net +75%. Per die: 5 x 1.75 = 8.75; 7 dice 61.25, rounded up to 62 (the costlier child, so it sets the container's cap requirement); needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 6 (cap 70), the Warlock's own level. A lesser Warlock may buy fewer dice.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Xenos",
								"Aeldari",
								"Psyker"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mDjkeqGTKUiIbPX47",
									"name": "Explosion",
									"cost_adj": "+50%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mxXnZM69DeIHmEesK",
									"name": "Armor Divisor (2)",
									"cost_adj": "+50%"
								},
								{
									"id": "m7Opi9axNrlja_z7t",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "m3CsaPV_KXVbGR2-z",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
									"cost_adj": "-5%"
								}
							],
							"points_per_level": 5,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 7
						},
						{
							"id": "t07sY2hqvqKdzLtxU",
							"name": "Embolden",
							"local_notes": "Lore: A wash of certainty over a willing ally that drives out fear for a few crucial moments.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10) delivering a 4-point Fearlessness 2 advantage (B55, 2/level), Warp Sorcery (-20%), Perils (Aeldari Runes, -5%). Net -20%. Full modified cost: 10 x 0.8 = 8 points (discounted to a fifth as the cheaper alternative ability); needs Aeldari Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20) at its full-price rate.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Xenos",
								"Aeldari",
								"Psyker"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mAKNLJJhpR24D6Zfn",
									"name": "Advantage Delivered (Emboldened",
									"cost_adj": "+5%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mEj7xU-XzRmFD0yOK",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mjEoq6LuWf2_yiuKL",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp (Aeldari Runes)",
									"cost_adj": "-5%"
								}
							],
							"base_points": 10
						}
					]
				}
			]
		}
	],
	"skills": [
		{
			"id": "sorjRbcu12Tm3YT92",
			"name": "Psyniscience",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The trained (or instinctive) sense of \"something wrong\" in a presence, place, or object touched by the warp — a chill in a corridor, a servitor's dead eyes going wrong. Named for the Dark Heresy/Only War skill of the same purpose (Psyniscience), used here for calibration only; the GURPS build is original.\n\nDesign: New skill per framework.md (\"New skills only when nothing fits\"). Per/H with no default: nobody can roll it untrained. Characters with a Psyker Talent (see the psyker power library, not part of this file) get it at a discount per that trait's rules. An unaugmented human without any psychic Talent has nothing latent to sense with and must buy it as an unusual background purchase, if a GM allows it at all; most unaugmented Imperial citizens simply never take this skill.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Psionic"
			],
			"difficulty": "per/h",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "s0pUKB-k6QSHHGC-3",
			"name": "Meditation",
			"reference": "B207",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The discipline that keeps a Warlock's gift steady under fire, without which no Aeldari psyker lasts long.\n\nDesign: Will+0 for 4 points, Hard; Meditation is Will-based (B207).",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"difficulty": "will/h",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sI7VFJoiAa4t0f-xr",
			"name": "Hidden Lore",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Warlock's real, Seer-Council-taught understanding of the immaterium, well beyond a Guardian's folk knowledge.\n\nDesign: IQ+1 (14) for 4 points, Average.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"specialization": "(the Warp)",
			"difficulty": "iq/a",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "s8p9EeuxV-F73ouyC",
			"name": "Guns",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Warlock still carries and uses a shuriken catapult like any other Guardian.\n\nDesign: DX+2 (16) for 4 points, Easy.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"specialization": "Rifle",
			"difficulty": "dx/e",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sA4W8x0D5W_h1NDHO",
			"name": "Broadsword",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The witchblade, a Warlock's own force weapon, carried and drilled with as seriously as any Aspect Warrior's blade.\n\nDesign: DX+2 (16) for 8 points, Average; the framework's las/plasma/melta and chainsword/power-sword weapon-skill table places force weapons on Broadsword/Staff/Axe, matched here to Broadsword.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 8
		},
		{
			"id": "s749DzwtFX-vKLF-E",
			"name": "Leadership",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Warlock is typically the senior figure attached to a Guardian defense force or Aspect warhost detachment.\n\nDesign: IQ+1 (14) for 4 points, Average.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"difficulty": "iq/a",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "shfoBykoGNuP6_TgQ",
			"name": "Tactics",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Enough battlefield sense to know when to spend a Rune of Battle and when to hold it.\n\nDesign: IQ+0 (13) for 4 points, Hard.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"difficulty": "iq/h",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sYH0v0l_q-mtLGYFW",
			"name": "Innate Attack",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Aiming a Destructor through the press of a firefight, drilled alongside the Guardian's catapult.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Beam) (DX/E, B201) at DX+2 (16) for 4 points, Easy; the skill Destructor's Burning Innate Attack build calls for.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"specialization": "Beam",
			"difficulty": "dx/e",
			"points": 4
		}
	],
	"equipment": []
